    "lectureTitle": "Differential Equations and Euler Simulation",
    "moduleId": "L03-M2",
    "title": "Exact exponential decay versus Euler approximation",
    "alt": "Comparison of the exact solution of first-order exponential decay with Euler points using a step equal to half the time constant",
    "caption": "For τ dx/dt=−x, forward Euler advances one step along the current tangent. With Δt=τ/2 it is stable, but at finite step size it decays faster than the exact exponential. Reducing Δt moves the discrete points toward the exact curve.",
