    "moduleId": "L04-M2",
    "title": "Current conservation in the membrane equivalent circuit",
    "alt": "Equivalent-circuit flow diagram in which applied current splits into capacitive current and ionic-channel currents at the membrane node",
    "caption": "Node conservation divides the applied current into two parts: C dVₘ/dt changes the charge stored across the membrane, while ΣGₓ(Vₘ−Eₓ) flows through ionic branches. Eₓ sets the zero-current voltage of a branch, and Gₓ sets how strongly that branch pulls Vₘ toward Eₓ.",
