    "lectureTitle": "Neural Networks I: Spike Representation, Convolution, and E/I Balance",
    "moduleId": "L08-M3",
    "title": "A strongly coupled network retains finite fluctuations after balance",
    "alt": "Flow diagram in which many excitatory and inhibitory spikes are filtered into large opposing inputs that cancel in the net input",
    "caption": "Under W∼1/√N, the conditional means of excitatory and inhibitory input are each O(√N) and must cancel at leading order. Their instantaneous difference remains O(1), so net input is not zero at every instant and can continue to drive irregular spiking.",
